{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_082fb5b31269dcbddacc35cf9e72974486d72f93a293a063e22a61500756edcd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a0e39033ecf41b20e20fe78d438b02750f8340a01a2ba745b310305e2a1f23a4"],"source_ids":["src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"The repository is a pnpm monorepo with packages for shared protocol types, mDNS discovery, a Fastify daemon, a Cloudflare Worker relay, a deploy-relay npx CLI, the loopsy CLI, an MCP server, a dashboard, and a Flutter mobile app.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3e1b96832e6506e7a62c205732b85f78cc5c21c2022cacc72feb660c4cc14547","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f6eff97305d813fa8b3846c5471a94bf8b820478532a2eda690cf83ce9687255","slc_fe93766bef321510c74c4cff5303a17c1d76eca5bd0ac4e67aa994081051fc75"],"source_ids":["src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"The daemon binds to 127.0.0.1 by default; LAN exposure for peer-to-peer is opt-in via `loopsy start --lan` or setting server.host to 0.0.0.0 in config.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_47d4107dfde5c40e1fabdb13267b5f0d6c1f6ee6b7bbfdd9dd4a177f86e0492f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1bd72c86b5350a7770b336e2ce54c55b3d79d0e1f8d58ea13cf0a8b4d51d47f0","slc_6b5eaefe840d66f1d2467ae169099ad36cdcc5077714ca8447e5966868a67216"],"source_ids":["src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"Phone control works by the daemon opening an outbound WebSocket to a Cloudflare Worker (Durable Object) that the phone also connects to; the Worker splices the two connections, requiring no port forwarding, public IP, or VPN.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4fe1ee2828a8dd54ffdc4835c4e6e7d7afec27ab134d46c6778a2f9865f72b90","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0afeb883b2a402920ea93ebd3693e894c1359de69126bd7bc1f5348879350eb7","slc_702eb077728217d83da06d65d79fe864a74417805a534e3c4f598ec4ca641bbe","slc_92e3aa995beacd46fed51ad293235f096e1721c90d71d120b191a76e5705d0c8"],"source_ids":["src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"Self-hosting the relay uses the @loopsy/deploy-relay npx CLI, which runs wrangler deploy against the user's Cloudflare account; Workers free tier and SQLite-backed Durable Objects are stated to cover personal use.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_58118e66b9cdd82cfe274b076ab84c4f2078146c0307351b4fd3fb416757e0a8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_cb91f02ea23efa473fe5ec0ab3b0256747b626e86a5a0c16834765732ad30e94"],"source_ids":["src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"When wired into an agent, the Loopsy MCP server exposes tools for peer listing, remote command execution, long-lived PTY sessions, file transfer, a shared key/value context store, messaging with ACKs, and read receipts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5b3b5433c2b48c40bfd491696a0965a9ad702eab4ddace943cb84072138d513e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_05ef7d8280d2c1bc83eabcfb9309cc4c45de0432c72efb4c9bf4ceaa3e3e3cf3","slc_4e52b7d2218847a769d8e7483274ac89e9146d5c5478f7a4125ea87a369ce92a","slc_61913cdadbebeca91139bf525a1a8e71d689a14d7b7d2b53b8618ae1c2ac3ac9","slc_a168dd4e96947b086d125d732168891978761093efacfb75f5ef691eff8a9820"],"source_ids":["src_085696af2bef502ca171cf04604f091b","src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"State lives under ~/.loopsy/ in config.yaml, context.json (key-value store), peers.json, logs/audit.jsonl, and relay.json; the messaging protocol stores inbox, outbox, and ack entries as context keys with TTLs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5f9ce24018cc75edd9deb13c9921776fbd31ff6592b58cd100a1138be9c84fb7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_be0f3f02176c5dc930805f3d4faa5926870b85dac21ad1b5caddd0443e8993c9","slc_f49bf2b0bcff7f11e42fdd1784c450915d1ebbc965ba142a4af21aec1fdf41c8"],"source_ids":["src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"TLS terminates at the relay, so the relay operator can read and modify terminal traffic including passwords; end-to-end phone-daemon encryption is deferred to the v1.1 roadmap, and self-hosting is the recommended mitigation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6abd789d7c4143b4e0caaa939e5f35d6046a9126e0cd0ef2f815090bdba1d4df","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6d16d10077e900bf13605dd782b7a40cc034dafc5ad2af0d7ddb43596e71a2af","slc_9eac0f397bd56dc603444f5c089bd0598383a5634b7d62cffd7dffc2ce42c98c","slc_b47959fc0c5b4113286207c57384b40d37f5117b5ba7ae086b9473a89721781f"],"source_ids":["src_085696af2bef502ca171cf04604f091b","src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors build with pnpm install and pnpm build, and releases are tag-driven — pushing a v* tag publishes loopsy and @loopsy/deploy-relay to npm via OIDC Trusted Publisher with provenance attestations.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7ed2a853df3eaec0eaf7a08ea589d8face604ff2548673bd6e7d14920ee87c89","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0e25726d8305f4098b155e377d7e6d3131a67b33c6533742e66fbe158e14e096","slc_c2a48e30eadf14532d3b05a319a4ad59041fd48b2c98207686396addbc9d2657"],"source_ids":["src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"Security design includes HMAC-signed pair tokens, SHA-256 hashing of secrets at rest, bearer tokens carried in Sec-WebSocket-Protocol headers rather than query strings, and constant-time bearer comparison.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_963e359ee9cecdd0a6126206d6b8d4316b952e002d4e41c54a025c89f094dedf","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2d2900d9a8f58f13352f14097b176b84ec9f891b85e00a1c071e3b58e74e22df","slc_b6de21b376603f45e8ab087770c6715fbbebb952cc0488c747ba41e070201588","slc_fd80f1eec0a7fbe5547af4ea70d1bbd2ee14e116d685e4cdbcea4429e679e1c3"],"source_ids":["src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"The loopsy CLI includes daemon lifecycle commands (init, start, stop, status, doctor, enable/disable), phone pairing and revocation, relay reconfiguration, log viewing, and API-key show/rotate commands.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c020f1519a5e914fc2bece30e49ad0c67463d446fb129949d73266a50f681f14","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"leox255/loopsy@73c165476279 snapshot 1ed6aebb8112bb9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_164543b02a441a2e9835391ab6031d9fc754f93e14407f0a2fac71e35e0e6273","slc_8a81f7c009badff8f513da3c71c2b069ba4540a3a84c4446434d8d03005f0410","slc_e9e65764d3b6c5c2b69f7891971ee1ea2b5095f263a7fd2bd4828f02ba288fbf"],"source_ids":["src_77f076c532035df782321748248e8689"],"text":"Per-session auto-approve lets a user opt in to skipping agent confirmation prompts; it defaults to off and enabling it the first time requires a macOS confirmation dialog (the user's password).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4a296e7043f496c926230455a40ba41"}
